t":"பெறுக","lemma":"பெறு","gloss":"may you obtain"}],"gloss":"may you obtain"},{"surface":"தில்","parts":[{"text":"தில்","lemma":"தில்","gloss":"particle of desire"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"நீயே","parts":[{"text":"நீயே","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you yourself"},{"surface":"வளஞ்சால்","parts":[{"text":"வளம்","lemma":"வளம்","gloss":"wealth"},{"text":"சால்","lemma":"சால்","gloss":"abundant"}],"gloss":"abundant in wealth"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"துளிபதன்","parts":[{"text":"துளி","lemma":"துளி","gloss":"rain drop"},{"text":"பதன்","lemma":"பதம்","gloss":"proper time"}],"gloss":"proper time of rain"},{"surface":"அறிந்து","parts":[{"text":"அறிந்து","lemma":"அறி","gloss":"having known"}],"gloss":"knowing"},{"surface":"பொழிய","parts":[{"text":"பொழிய","lemma":"பொழி","gloss":"to shower"}],"gloss":"to shower"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வேலி","parts":[{"text":"வேலி","lemma":"வேலி","gloss":"veli (measure of land)"}],"gloss":"velis"},{"surface":"ஆயிரம்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயிரம்","lemma":"ஆயிரம்","gloss":"thousand"}],"gloss":"a thousand"},{"surface":"விளைக","parts":[{"text":"விளைக","lemma":"விளை","gloss":"may it yield"}],"gloss":"may it yield"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"வயலே","parts":[{"text":"வயல்","lemma":"வயல்","gloss":"field"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis particle"}],"gloss":"fields indeed"}]}],"literal":"Cool drops many showering, the cloud sounds / like a mountain-peak touching the sky / high-rising paddy, to the delight of / the bulls that brought great wealth, praising and receiving / the unrefined strong toddy, spreading out and digging / drinking the toddy, they rejoice happily / because the northern land of Venkatam is hungry / coming here and staying, my very large family / to relieve their hunger, the ancient lineage of good character / in the wide, ancient town, when I asked / 'He has no relatives who came before, and yet / he is a pitiable one, a singer is he,' thus / those who know you, knowing me, said / I have come to see you, O Lord, with great dignity / in the great backwaters of deep water, eating the fish / the birds with dense feathers sleep / in the beautiful city of dense punnai trees / with your beloved wife who resides in your heart / may you obtain sweet sleep, you who are full of wealth / knowing the right time of rain to shower / may a thousand velis of land yield in your fields!","translation":"While clouds rumble and pour cool drops of rain, the heaps of paddy rise as high as sky-touching mountain peaks. The farmers praise the great wealth brought by their plowing bulls, dig out jars of unrefined strong toddy, and drink it with joy. Because the northern lands beyond the Venkatam hills were struck by famine, my large family of kinsmen came here to seek refuge. When I inquired in this ancient, spacious town, the noble-hearted locals, recognizing my poverty, spoke of my plight to you. Hearing this, I have come to see you, O Lord! In your fertile town surrounded by dense punnai trees, where water-fowls with thick feathers sleep after feeding on fish in the deep backwaters, may you enjoy sweet sleep with your beloved wife who dwells in your heart. Knowing the right season, may the rains pour, and may a thousand velis of land yield rich harvests in your fields!","modern":"குளிர்ந்த துளிகளைப் பலவாகப் பொழிந்து மேகம் முழங்கும். விண்முட்டும் மலை போன்ற நெற்குவியல்கள் உயர்ந்துள்ளன. உழவு எருதுகள் தந்த பெருவளத்தைப் போற்றிப் பெற்ற, வடிகட்டாத கள்ளினைத் தோண்டி எடுத்து, அதனைப் பருகி மகிழ்வர். வேங்கட மலைக்கு அப்பாலுள்ள வடநாடு பசியால் வாடியதால், இங்கு வந்து தங்கிய என் பெரிய சுற்றம் பசி தீர உதவும் நற்பண்புடைய பழங்குடிகள் வாழும் இப்பழைய ஊரில் நான் விசாரித்தேன். 'முன்பின் தெரியாதவன், வறியவன், இவன் ஒரு பாணன்' என்று உன்னை அறிந்தவர்கள் என் நிலையை உன்னிடம் கூறினர். அதைக் கேட்டு உன்னைக் காண வந்தேன் தலைவனே! ஆழமான நீரையுடைய பெரிய கழியில் மீன்களை உண்டு, அடர்ந்த சிறகுகளையுடைய பறவைகள் தங்கும் புன்னை மரங்கள் சூழ்ந்த அழகிய நகரில், உன் நெஞ்சிற்கு இனிய மனைவியோடு நீ இனிதே துயில்வாயாக! மழைக்காலம் அறிந்து பெய்ய, உனது வயல்களில் ஆயிரம் வேலி நெல் விளையட்டும்!","explanation":"This poem is composed by Kalladanar in praise of Poraiyatru Kizhan, a generous chieftain of Poraiyaru. The poet describes how his large family of singers and kinsmen fled the famine-stricken northern region of Venkatam and sought refuge in the chieftain's fertile territory. Upon inquiring in the ancient town, the locals recognized the poet's poverty and recommended him to the chieftain, prompting this visit. The poet praises the chieftain's fertile land, where birds rest in dense punnai trees after feeding on fish in the backwaters. He concludes with a heartfelt blessing, wishing the chieftain sweet sleep with his beloved wife and a bountiful harvest of a thousand velis of paddy in his fields.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.5],[1.5,1.8],[1.8,1.8],[1.8,3.0],[3.0,3.0],[3.0,3.5],[3.5,3.7],[3.7,3.7],[3.7,5.6],[5.6,5.8],[5.8,6.51],[6.51,7.22],[7.22,7.7],[7.7,8.57],[8.7,8.9],[8.9,9.8],[9.8,10.0],[10.0,10.83],[10.87,11.0],[11.0,11.73],[11.86,12.22],[12.4,12.6],[12.6,12.9],[12.9,13.1],[13.1,14.3],[14.3,14.4],[14.4,14.8],[14.8,15.7],[15.88,16.8],[16.8,17.4],[17.4,17.6],[17.6,18.0],[18.72,19.22],[19.22,19.62],[19.62,19.92],[19.92,20.22],[20.22,20.92],[20.92,21.07],[21.12,21.72],[21.72,22.62],[22.62,22.82],[22.82,23.42],[23.46,23.72],[23.72,24.72],[24.72,24.72],[24.72,25.32],[25.32,26.02],[26.02,26.22],[26.37,27.42],[27.42,27.42],[27.42,28.52],[28.52,28.72],[29.32,29.92],[29.92,30.57],[30.57,30.68],[30.68,31.02],[31.02,31.98],[31.98,32.31],[32.55,32.82],[32.82,33.12],[33.12,33.92],[33.92,34.12],[34.12,34.12],[34.12,35.22],[36.04,36.64],[36.64,37.14],[37.14,37.64],[37.64,37.74],[37.74,39.31],[39.34,39.74],[39.74,39.99],[40.19,40.44],[40.44,41.34],[41.34,41.84],[41.84,42.24],[42.24,42.53],[42.6,42.74],[42.74,43.94],[43.94,44.44],[44.44,45.24],[45.24,45.44],[45.44,45.74],[45.74,46.04],[46.04,46.24]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,